===Appearance===
The appearance of Torva armour was graphically updated on 3 August 2023, as it was believed to have clashed with the "simple and bold aesthetics" of Old School's art style. The level of detail of the original was designed for the larger world scale of ''RuneScape'', and thus was believed to have appeared "cluttered and out-of place".

A non-trivial number of players disagreed with said change, mostly due to nostalgia towards its iconic appearance in its original release in RuneScape 2 in 2011. As such, [[unobtainable]] variants of the [[Torva full helm (unobtainable item)|full helm]], [[Torva platebody (unobtainable item)|platebody]], and [[Torva platelegs (unobtainable item)|platelegs]] were released as a compromise to allow the third party client [[RuneLite]] to use the assets for various plugins which changed the appearance of the player character (such as [https://runelite.net/plugin-hub/show/fashionscape Fashionscape] and [https://runelite.net/plugin-hub/show/weapon-animation-replacer Weapon/Gear/Animation Replacer]), although other players would not be able to see said player overriding their appearance:

